{"term":"purple","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:a126d9a8daf4963849","definition":"A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","example":"Arraying with reflected Purple and Gold / The Clouds that on his Weſtern Throne attend.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["blue-red"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:23a31a843775c439af","definition":"Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:814b16970ffecd07fa","definition":"Cloth, or a garment, dyed a purple colour; especially, a purple robe, worn as an emblem of rank or authority; specifically, the purple robe or mantle worn by Ancient Roman emperors as the emblem of imperial dignity.","example":"to put on the imperial purple","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bdd759f4c92c295140","definition":"Imperial power.","example":"1776-1788, Edward Gibbon, The History of the Decline and Fall of the Roman Empire\nHe was born in the purple.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly","register":"broadly, countable, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktio